,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833745543,"data":"Solve $4+x=4$ for $x$. You have access to `math`, `numpy`, and `sympy` for:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833749829,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833751411,"data":"# Symbolic Computation (sympy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833752564,"data":"- Algebraic manipulation and simplification\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833753811,"data":"- Solving equations and systems of equations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833754962,"data":"- Symbolic differentiation and integration\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833756296,"data":"- Number theory functions (primes, divisors, modular arithmetic)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833757511,"data":"- Polynomial operations and factorization\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833758666,"data":"- Working with mathematical expressions symbolically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833759841,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833760987,"data":"# Numerical Computation (numpy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833762108,"data":"- Array operations and linear algebra\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833763222,"data":"- Efficient numerical calculations for large datasets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833764411,"data":"- Matrix operations and eigenvalue problems\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833765605,"data":"- Statistical computations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833766765,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833767821,"data":"# Mathematical Functions (math):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833768933,"data":"- Standard mathematical functions (trig, log, exp)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833770132,"data":"- Constants like pi and e\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833771236,"data":"- Basic operations for single values\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.83377237,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833773435,"data":"Best Practices:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833774814,"data":"- Use sympy for exact symbolic answers when possible\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833776082,"data":"- Use numpy for numerical verification and large-scale computation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833777699,"data":"- Combine symbolic and numerical approaches: derive symbolically, verify numerically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833778937,"data":"- Document your computational strategy clearly\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833780081,"data":"- Validate computational results against known cases or theoretical bounds\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833781323,"data":"- For very large exponents (e.g. a^(n!)), use pow(base, exp, mod) or analytical methods — never materialize the full number\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833782665,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833783863,"data":"# Code Robustness Rules:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833785175,"data":"- Each code cell must be SELF-CONTAINED: re-import and re-define everything you need. If a previous cell errored, its definitions are LOST.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833786546,"data":"- Avoid sympy expressions that grow beyond a few hundred characters. If an expression is exploding, switch to numerical methods (numpy) or modular arithmetic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833787923,"data":"- For geometry: prefer numpy coordinate models with brute-force verification over pure symbolic or direction-counting approaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833789239,"data":"- For combinatorics counting: always verify no duplicates — check injectivity explicitly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833790519,"data":"- If 5+ code cells without progress, STOP and restart with a different approach.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.83379388,"data":"- When using Python, prefer converting sympy expressions to int() before passing to Python builtins like pow(), min(), max().\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833795222,"data":"- Common import: from sympy.ntheory.modular import crt (note: sympy.crt does not exist).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.83379646,"data":"- If a code cell fails, re-import necessary libraries in the next cell.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833797714,"data":"- sympy.solve() often times out on complex systems. For polynomial systems with \u003e 3 unknowns, prefer numerical methods (scipy fsolve/minimize) or manual algebraic reduction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833799172,"data":"- Never call sympy.simplify() or sympy.expand() on expressions involving large binomials or products of many terms. Use float() first to check the numerical value.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":511.833800881,"data":"\n"}
